It does and it doesn't.

The fire_damage() function doesn't consider fireproofing for containers, 
scrolls, spellbooks and potions except that scroll of fire, spellbook of 
fireball and the Book of Dead are immune.

Other items that are flammable check fireproofing before burn damage is 
applied. Flammable items are items that are of these materials: wax, 
vegetation, flesh, paper, cloth, leather, wood or plastic, unless it 
convoys fire resistance or is a wand of fire.

Unless item breaks when it is thrown, kicked or dropped from height the 
damage sustained from ending in lava square is the same as in normal drop.

Topi

